  "query_preview": "..Gusty east winds have been cranking up since late\nlast night with some of the highest gusts between 55 and 75 mph\nas of 230 am. VAD wind profiles on Tucson radar (KEMX) showed\nE-SE winds up to 50 kts between 6k and 8k feet. Surface pressure\ndifference across the area was around 12 mbs. Early morning\nsatellite imagery was showing brief periods of lenticular \ncloud development over some of the mountains. Strongest winds \nare expected later this morning as the gradient tightens between\nupper low off the northern Baja coast and the 1040 to 1043 mb \nsurface high across the Colorado front range. High Wind Warning\nand Wind Advisory remain in effect for today into Saturday.\n\nThe above mentioned upper low will pull in remnant moisture \nfrom decaying tropical storm Simon, which was south of Cabo\nthis morning, over the next 24 hours. This upper low will then \nlift and open up across Arizona Sunday and Monday and bring a \nchance of showers, possibly an isolated thunderstorm, to SE AZ. \nA slow moving Pacific upper level trof will keep unsettled \nconditions Tuesday into early next week with daily chances of \nshowers (20-50 percent) each day. Daily high temperatures will \nremain below normal for much of the next 7 days.",
